16. Fractional viewport boundaries
Use non-integer samplesPerPixel, such as 1.5f, and a non-zero firstSampleIndex. Verify columns are included only when their half-open display ranges truly intersect the pixel range.
17. Viewport change does not stale current jobs
Start with viewport A and schedule visible columns 0, 1, 2. Before workers complete, switch to viewport B where those columns are offscreen but the config/generation is unchanged. Complete the old jobs. Verify they are allowed to commit, but may be evicted according to latest visibility and cache pressure.
18. Latest visibility controls eviction
Use maxCachedColumns = 2. Schedule columns while viewport A is visible, then switch to viewport B before completion. Complete old jobs out of order. Verify eviction protects columns visible in viewport B, not columns that were visible when the jobs were scheduled.
19. Snapshot marks used for LRU
Commit columns 0, 1, and 2 with maxCachedColumns = 3. Call renderSnapshot with a viewport that reads column 0. Then pan and commit a new offscreen column under cache pressure. Verify column 0 is treated as recently used and a less-recent non-visible column is evicted first.
20. Compose scheduling only through composition
Do not call any internal scheduling method. Set content with ProgressiveSpectrogram(state, Modifier.size(...)), run Compose/main-thread work, and verify pending jobs appear. Recompose several times with the same state and size. Verify no duplicate jobs are submitted.
